# A material graph in the Graph panel (ADR 0211), on a copy of
# examples/23-surfaces: the dissolve made again as nodes, opened by its name;
# a link that cannot be made, tried; the list a node is added from, typed
# into; and a line of an expression typed wrong, saved and compiled, so the
# compiler's error is on its node. The docks are pulled back first, so the
# canvas has room to be read. Coordinates are a 1600 by 900 frame's.
wait 60
drag 700 607 700 820
wait 6
drag 1247 300 1480 300
wait 6
key ctrl+p
wait 8
text dissolve-graph.surfacegraph
wait 10
key enter
wait 20
idle
shot surface-open
# Base's colour, three wide, into the surface's alpha, which is a number.
drag 877 350 1049 437
wait 4
shot surface-refused
# A right press where nothing is: the list, and two letters typed into it.
rclick 500 700
wait 6
text no
wait 6
shot surface-list
key escape
wait 4
# The expression chosen, its line typed over, the graph saved: `idle` waits
# for the compiler, however long this machine's takes.
click 800 481
wait 4
dbl 1380 314
wait 4
key ctrl+a
wait 2
text a * nothingCalledThis
wait 4
key enter
wait 6
click 600 720
wait 4
key ctrl+s
idle
wait 6
shot surface-error
quit
